  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "/6LXsLu6MFrLKIhBM2x6LA0IXKI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:31:46.274Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "MHP's tool field records one platform, SAP, against two verticals, automotive and manufacturing. That is a clear reading for a rescore that weighs slot occupancy: the platform slot is filled, and it is filled by the vendor whose ecosystem defines how German automotive and manufacturing back offices are built.\n\nThe narrowness cuts both ways. A firm concentrated on one platform and two adjacent sectors is easy to characterise and easy to exclude, but it also has no second slot in which a different kind of component could sit without touching the SAP practice.\n\nAs with the other carried-over rows, the tier is mechanical rather than evidenced: a provisional v2 tail entry, rescored on size and slot occupancy, never scored on v3, with the OSS-portfolio screen the flag asks for still outstanding.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- MHP (DE)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Automotive, manufacturing",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:31:46.274930Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:31:46.274933Z"
    }
  },
